{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790361399,"nonce":"xcg43LG6ikQQgLQZfPxiMF+Ir/k=","title":"LLVM tier: performs ignore with scopes and handler state, and async slot ops have no lowering","message":"`compile_instruction` in crates/compiler/src/llvm_backend.rs lowers `PerformEffect` as a direct call to the handler found in `effect_handler_index`, which `lower_module` builds from `module.handlers` with the last matching handler winning. It never calls `__zyntax_effect_lookup_op` or `__zyntax_effect_lookup_state`, so code the LLVM tier compiles ignores `with` scopes, passes no `self` to an operation of a stateful effect, and can pick a different default handler from Cranelift, which takes the first declared. `AsyncSaveSlot`, `AsyncLoadSlot` and `IndirectCall` have no arm and fail with \"Instruction not yet implemented\", so neither a poll function nor a resumable perform site can be compiled by LLVM. Nothing in `TieredBackend` keeps effectful functions off the LLVM tier. Found by reading; not reproduced under `TieredRuntime::production_llvm()`.\n\nDone: the LLVM `PerformEffect` arm matches Cranelift's (the `select(lookup_op != 0, dyn, static)` dispatch, `self` from `lookup_state` under the effect-level ABI, first-declared static default), the slot ops and `IndirectCall` have arms, and the effect, fiber and async composition tests under crates/zynml/tests pass with the LLVM tier forced on.","files":null}]}